# An and with a mask of several runs of bits is the sum of each run's
# bits, x mod 2^top − x mod 2^low, as 32- and 64-bit masks up to the top
# bit; a value negative on some threads keeps its sign through a run to
# the top bit, read as mul.wide.s32 reads it and refused by mul.wide.u32.
# In a mask of more runs, a run that clears bit 31 of a parameter, whose
# range is unknown, is its remainder mod 2^31. A run from bit 63 above a
# clear bit 62 and a remainder whose modulus does not divide the form's
# offset stay unknown.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/and_runs.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_and_dc
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 4–5 sectors (ideal 1)
CHECK-SAME: [16 * ⌊(%tid.x mod 32)/4⌋ + 256 * ⌊(%tid.x mod 256)/64⌋ + param_0]
CHECK: kernel micro_and_46
CHECK: st.global.u16  global store 2 B  warp: 1–2 sectors (ideal 1)
CHECK-SAME: [128 * ⌊(%tid.x mod 64)/32⌋ + 4 * (%tid.x mod 4) + param_0]
CHECK: kernel micro_and_top
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 2–3 sectors (ideal 2)
CHECK-SAME: [1024 * ⌊%tid.x/256⌋ + 4 * (%tid.x mod 16) + param_0]
CHECK: kernel micro_and_wide
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 2–3 sectors (ideal 2)
CHECK-SAME: [1024 * ⌊%tid.x/256⌋ + 4 * (%tid.x mod 16) + param_0]
CHECK: kernel micro_and_bit63
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
CHECK-SAME: unknown: and-mask 0x80000000000000ff keeps bit 63 without 62
CHECK: kernel micro_and_offset
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
CHECK-SAME: unknown: depends on special register %tid.x, in a mod
CHECK: kernel micro_and_top_signed
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 2–3 sectors (ideal 2)
CHECK-SAME: [1024 * ⌊%tid.x/256⌋ + 4 * (%tid.x mod 16) + param_0 - 1024]
CHECK: kernel micro_and_top_unsigned
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B
CHECK-SAME: unknown: `mul.wide.u32` reads a value its type does not hold
CHECK: kernel micro_and_sign_runs
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)
CHECK-SAME: [param_0 + 4 * (param_1 mod 16) + 4 * (param_1 mod 2147483648) - 4 * (param_1 mod 256)]
